                <pb facs="0213" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg153"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 2379.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Hixson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-30"><hi rendition="#small-caps">September</hi> 30,
                            1895</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Have made urgent representations to the Tsung-li Yamên to issue orders to the
                    viceroy to cease to impede your efforts, and to order his subordinates to assist
                    you in every way. Viceroy of Szechuan has been degraded and made forever
                    incapable of holding office. Subordinates will be punished. Quote the
                    example.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Denby</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
